From cfcf373062542f2bf0cb90f271dfffd1df82b79c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:05:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(es): Require full-width trace and span IDs when reading
 from Elasticsearch

dbmodel.TraceID.ToOTEL and dbmodel.SpanID.ToOTEL used to left-pad shorter
hex strings with zeros. Every ES/OS writer goes through pdata and stores
32-char trace IDs and 16-char span IDs, so the padding only served legacy
short-form data. Make both conversions strict about width and drop the
unused 16-character core fixtures.

Part of #9717 (M4).
